# The published tree is about 16 MB, so nothing currently needs LFS.
#
# An earlier version of this file had "*.asset filter=lfs", which was wrong:
# Unity *.asset files include the baked NavMesh data, some of which is 314 MB
# in a single file. LFS hides the size from the 100 MB hard limit but not from
# the quota, and it was only masking files that should never have been
# committed at all. Those bakes are now excluded in .gitignore.
#
# These rules exist so that if original-resolution art is ever added back, it
# routes through LFS automatically instead of failing the push.
*.tif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.psd filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Normalise line endings: Unity asset files are binary-ish, scripts are not.
*.cs text eol=lf
*.meta text eol=lf
